{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838119-haaaaalp-new-calais-freehold-is-non-existant","id":838119,"title":"HAAAAALP! New Calais Freehold is non-existant.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-27T10:08:20-08:00","id":838119,"title":"HAAAAALP! New Calais Freehold is non-existant.","content":"Back in first edition the players and I used the Seasonal Courts because it was the easiest thing to do and the players only had access to the core book at home and had chosen Courts based on it. The game, being based in Louisiana never quite felt like it fit. Now I guess I could use the Tornado/flood seasons from Winter Masques as a quick cheat, it still feels kinda meh.<br /> <br /> Now, here's where things got weird: One thing that the players and I latched onto was &quot;what if the changeling didn't choose their court&quot;. this was our &quot;big change&quot; from the base rules. A changeling could chose to 'side' with a court through goodwill but a changeling was &quot;marked&quot; the moment they fell through the hedge.<br /> <br /> Last week during Character Creation we played with the idea of &quot;Directional&quot; courts, but it felt forced, I've also thought about doing &quot;regions&quot; based on the source of the eponymous &quot;Mist&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh yeah: The city in the Mist gains its name from the fact that the city is forever being 'invaded&quot; by a sickly green mist that seeps in from trods, it usually in small amounts, and from certain natural sources, the River, the Swamp, the Parks and the Cemetaries. this MIst grows thicker when the Gentry and their Servants are near (and in 2007 it covered the whole of the city and left many of the older Lost dead or gone as a veritable army of huntsmen took the city by storm.)<br /> <br /> Okay, Here's what I got:<br /> <br /> So here's what I got:<br /> <br /> The Bulwark is found in the Census, which occurs on the new year. During that time the Courts' tally their members and the Court with the most surviving members rules for the following year. I'm not sold on it being a full year, but the idea is that the fact that city being willing to allow the vagaries of fate to determine which court holds sway confuses and frightens the Gentry, keeping them at bay. The attack nearly 10 years ago was due to the fact that Eugene, the (then) Autumn King, was gaming the system by sending out loyal summer court thugs to scare off new members of the other courts as they appeared to hold power for 4 consecutive cycles, breaking the bulwark.<br /> <br /> Now, as I type this I think I do like the idea of Regional Courts (we'd called them Directional courts, but that was flawed). what do y'all think of this:<br /> <br /> The Grave Court; The Leaden Scepter, The Black Coven, The Court of Dread<br /> <br /> The River Court; The Roaring Trident; The Sapphire Phalanx, The Court of Rage<br /> <br /> The Swamp Court; The Honored Seat, The Gray Cavalry, The Court of Resentment<br /> <br /> The Garden Court; The Evergreen Throne; The Rose Kingdom, The Court of Hope<br /> <br /> Wow... that kinda just happened while typing this out.<br /> <br /> So anyway, when a Changeling crosses through the Hedge, they are marked by the emotion that drove them to flee arcadia, and by where they escape, marking them forever as a member of that court. When an outside Changeling enters the city... I don't know... maybe they're marked when they enter the Hedge... yeah that might work.<br /> <br /> How is this? Should I move forward? I worry that three of the courts are &quot;negative&quot; or that &quot;hope&quot; is too &quot;nice&quot;... thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":". 02-27-2016, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T11:04:16-08:00","id":838136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/838119-haaaaalp-new-calais-freehold-is-non-existant#post838119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is this? Should I move forward?</div> </div> </div> </div>The main problem that comes to mind is that the Bulwark ritual doesn't seem to have much of an actual input to mess with, particularly for a yearly feature. (For clarity's sake, this is operating at least partially on Second Edition conventions now, right?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I worry that three of the courts are &quot;negative&quot; or that &quot;hope&quot; is too &quot;nice&quot;... thoughts. </div> </div> </div>When I described the Seasonal Courts in fairly neutral terms to a friend with no knowledge of Changeling, she thought they sounded evil. Make of that what you will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T11:50:38-08:00","id":838153,"title":"","content":"Actually the Bulwark effect was added after reading the rules, originally we just used the seasonal courts rules (with the autumn court refusing to give up power and using force and promises of power to refuse the transfer of power.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Census is can be messed with a number of ways: Intimidation, violence and outright Lying (Declaring based on court good will... there'd have to be more to it than that, but the Grave Court is pretty damned trixy that way) I'll definitely take another look at it though.<br /> <br /> Here's what I came up with since though:<br /> <br /> <b>The Garden Court</b><br /> The Rose Salon, the Evergreen Throne, the Court of Want<br /> <br /> Contracts: Talespinning, Emotion (Want), Vainglory (\u2022\u2022-\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Mantle<br /> \u2022 +1 to Socialize Rolls to Carouse<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow (City Parks)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains the Barfly Merit<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains a personal Approach<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier Gains the Enchanted Performance \u2022\u2022\u2022 Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>The Grave Court</b><br /> The Black Coven, the Leaden Scepter, the Court of Dread<br /> <br /> Contracts: Talespinning, Emotion (Dread), Creeping Dread (\u2022)<br /> <br /> Mantle<br /> \u2022 +1 to rolls to study the Hedge, hobs, huntsmen and true fae<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow (Cemetaries)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains the Hob Kin Merit<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains a personal Approach<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gain 3 dots of the Hollow Merit, Even if this takes your character past 5 dots, they may use the bonus \u2018dots\u2019 to enhance their current hollow.<br /> <br /> <b>The River Court</b><br /> The Sapphire Phalanx, the Roaring Trident, the Court of Rage<br /> <br /> Contracts: Talespinning, Emotion (Rage), Know the Competition<br /> <br /> Mantle<br /> \u2022 The Courtier gains the Defensive Fighting Merit.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow (Rivers and Streams)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains a +1 to defense, even against ranged attacks.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains a personal Approach<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier Gains the Potent Kith \u2022\u2022\u2022 Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>The Swamp Court</b><br /> The Gray Cavalry, the Honored Seat, the Court of Resentment<br /> <br /> Contracts: Talespinning, Emotion (Resentment), Thorns and Brambles (\u2022\u2022)<br /> <br /> Mantle<br /> \u2022 Gain an additional door whenever someone attempts to talk them out of a course of action.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Goblin Vow (Swamps)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains the Gentrified Bearing Merit<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains a personal Approach<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The Courtier gains the Fae Mount Merit<br /> <br /> I'm still not thrilled with &quot;hope&quot; I see the Garden Court as the Court of manic partying, those that dance as the the city burns. I'm kinda going with a metaphor for the antebellum south (which is how long the freehold has existed) I thought about saying &quot;Hunger&quot; but hungering for Hunger seems... odd. The previous leader (when it was technically the spring court) was a Brewer called Tumbledown Tom who fed on the hopes and dreams of those who found themselves in his bar. He was fun and happy and the players loved hanging out with him, even when he was getting a groom-to-be plastered and supping on the boy's hopes/dreams/joy at the upcoming nuptuals. I guess their the Court of the future in that way.<br /> <br /> ... what if it was exuberance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":".  Changed Hope to Want 02-27-2016, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}